.TH geectl-build-download-binary 1  "geectl-build-download-binary 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-download\-binary \- Download one built file by name. With `\-\-all`, every built file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build download\-binary\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-output\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> [\fIFILENAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download one built file by name. With `\-\-all`, every built file
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Where to write the downloaded bytes: the file path (it must not already exist), or the directory every built file goes into with `\-\-all`
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Download every built file into the `\-\-output` directory; a file already there refuses the run. The downloads are sequential, not atomic: if one fails, the files already downloaded stay
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package the file belongs to
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the file was built in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the file was built for
.TP
[\fIFILENAME\fR]
The file to download (e.g. `foo\-1.0\-1.x86_64.rpm`). Required unless `\-\-all` downloads every built file
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
